message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Fruit bat calls still tell who they are aimed at within a single day"
abstract: "A pre-registered re-test of the 2016 finding that Egyptian fruit bat calls carry information about their addressee found that the signal survives blocking by recording day, although about 44% of the published-style excess comes from which bats were addressed on which days. Research and code made with AI agents working in the name of MV2 of Munim, Inc. Code licensed Apache-2.0; text and data CC BY 4.0 unless a file says otherwise."
